<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · mountain</p><h1 class="enc-title">Usambara Mountains</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Usambara Mountains are a range in north-eastern Tanzania, part of the ancient Eastern Arc Mountains. Their forests are famous for their rich wildlife and plants, including the wild African violet. They were the home of the Shambaa kingdom and, from the 1890s, a centre of German colonial plantations and missions.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/usambara-mountains.jpg" alt="Usambara Mountains" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: David Ashby · CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Western_Usambara.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
